# Power Query (M) ETL Documentation

This document outlines the Extract, Transform, and Load (ETL) pipeline built in **Power Query** to clean, consolidate, and standardize raw **GASTAT** and **GOSI** Excel workbooks (Q1 2021 – Q2 2026) before loading them into the Power BI data model.

## 1. ETL Pipeline Overview

---
| Stage | Key Transformations Applied |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Ingestion & Consolidation** | Combined multi-sheet annual workbooks (2021–2025) and quarterly-sheet workbooks (`القطاعات`, `التوزيع النسبي للبطالة للحاصلين على دبلوم فأعلى`, and `معدل البطالة للحاصلين على دبلوم فأعلى`) into unified fact tables using `Table.Combine` / Append Queries.
| **Header & Row Cleanup** | Removed report title banners and trailing blank rows, promoted actual column headers (`Table.PromoteHeaders`), and filtered out null records. |
| **Arabic Text Normalization** | Applied `Text.Trim` and `Text.Clean` across dimension columns and standardized inconsistent spellings across survey years (e.g., administrative region names and education labels). |
| **Date & Type Standardization** | Cast quarterly date keys (`الربع`) to `type date` to establish clean one-to-many relationships with the central `Calender` table, and enforced numeric types on all rate/count columns. |
| **Model Optimization** | Disabled load (`Enable Load = Off`) for staging queries and removed legacy unused sheets to keep the `.pbix` footprint lightweight. |

---

## 2. Key M-Code Snippets

### A. Multi-Sheet Quarterly Consolidation (Example: `القطاعات`)
*Dynamically reads all quarterly tabs from the workbook, promotes headers per sheet, appends them into one table, and enforces data types.*

```powerquery
let
    Source = Excel.Workbook(File.Contents(FilePath & "القطاعات"), null, true),
    FilteredSheets = Table.SelectRows(Source, each [Kind] = "Sheet"),
    CleanedSheets = Table.TransformColumns(
        FilteredSheets,
        {"Data", each Table.PromoteHeaders(_, [PromoteAllScalars=true])}
    ),
    ExpandedData = Table.Combine(CleanedSheets[Data]),
    TrimmedText = Table.TransformColumns(ExpandedData, {{"النشاط الاقتصادي", Text.Trim, type text}}),
    TypedColumns = Table.TransformColumnTypes(TrimmedText, {
        {"الربع", type date}
        // Add remaining numeric column types from your Advanced Editor
    })
in
    TypedColumns


# B. Standard Fact Table Cleaning (Example: البطالة)

let
    Source = Excel.Workbook(File.Contents(FilePath & "Saudi Labor Market.xlsx"), null, true),
    SheetData = Source{[Item="البطالة", Kind="Sheet"]}[Data],
    PromotedHeaders = Table.PromoteHeaders(SheetData, [PromoteAllScalars=true]),
    FilteredNulls = Table.SelectRows(PromotedHeaders, each [الربع] <> null),
    ChangedTypes = Table.TransformColumnTypes(FilteredNulls, {
        {"الربع", type date},
        {"سعوديون - ذكور", type number},
        {"سعوديون - إناث", type number},
        {"سعوديون - إجمالي", type number},
        {"الإجمالي - الكل", type number}
    })
in
    ChangedTypes


3. Data Quality Issues Resolved During ETL
Inconsistent Column Spacing: Standardized Arabic column headers with double spaces around hyphens across different yearly releases.

Spelling Variations Across Years: Unified region and education labels (e.g., harmonizing الحدود الشماليه / الحدود الشمالية and aligning legacy vs. revised education categories) so slicers and charts aggregate accurately.

Legacy Sheet Pruning: Audited and removed seven unused prototype sheets from the initial 2025 draft workbook (Saudi Labor Market.xlsx) so only active fact tables load into the final semantic model.
